    "result_text": "All tests pass (7 run, 0 failures). Let me verify the change is complete by confirming no other 400/409/429 rejection path escapes problem+json. I've already traced every 400/409/429 escalation handler; only `InvalidOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler` was non-conforming and is now fixed.\n\nThe change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe specification requires all rejection responses (400, 409, 429) to return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`.\n\n**What I found:** Every rejection handler already emitted a Spring `ProblemDetail` (which OfficeFloor serializes through Spring's return-value handlers, giving `application/problem+json` automatically) **except one** \u2014 the primary 400 path:\n\n- 400: `ValidationExceptionHandler` \u2713 already problem+json; `InvalidOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler` \u2717 returned a bespoke `{\"errors\":[...]}` body as `application/json`\n- 409: `CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`, `DuplicateOwnerIdentityExceptionHandler` \u2713\n- 429: `DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler` \u2713\n\nAll owner-field validation (missing/blank fields, email domain, postcode, future registration date) funnels through `InvalidOwnerFieldsException`, so that single handler was the whole gap \u2014 and exactly what the acceptance test exercises (a missing `city` \u2192 400).\n\n**The fix** (`InvalidOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler.java`): now builds its body via the shared `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper (same one every other handler uses \u2014 so `type`/`title`/`status`/`detail`/`timestamp` stay consistent) and populates `schemaValidationErrors` with a `ValidationMessageDto` per offending field, mirroring how `ValidationExceptionHandler` already reports Spring bean-validation failures. This preserves the field-name information the old body carried, in the standard structure, rather than duplicating logic or introducing a parallel format. I removed the now-unused bespoke `ValidationErrors` record.\n\n**Result:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS, 7 tests, 0 failures, including `coreRejectionIsProblemJson` which asserts the `application/problem+json` content type and `$.status == 400`.",
